    <p>
      I am finishing my B.Eng. in New Energy Science and Engineering (wind-energy track) at
      North China Electric Power University (expected June 2027), with an average of 82.9/100 and
      strong results in my wind-engineering specialization — Wind Turbine Aerodynamics (Excellent),
      Wind Resource Measurement &amp; Assessment (95/100), and Numerical Simulation (90/100).
    </p>
    <p>
      I am currently working on a <b>multi-timescale model of a direct-drive PMSG wind turbine</b> —
      a funded project at the National Key Laboratory of Renewable Energy Electric Systems,
      developing reduced-order average-value models for comparison with WECC Type 4 and
      IEC 61400-27-1 reference models for system-level grid-integration simulation. Before that,
      I completed <b>CFD simulations</b> of wind-turbine-relevant external flows
      (ANSYS Fluent, with the cylinder-flow case also run in OpenFOAM). My embedded and hardware
      background — including a <b>National First Prize</b> in the China Undergraduate
      Electronic Design Contest (power-monitoring circuit design and system integration) —
      backs the research with strong implementation ability, and I maintain a small portfolio
      of open hardware / edge-computing projects. I am looking for a fully funded
      PhD position (Fall 2027) in renewable-energy integration, wind-turbine modeling,
      and power-system simulation.
    </p>
