  <section id="research">
    <h2><span class="no">04</span>Research Experience<span class="rule"></span></h2>
    <div class="item">
      <div class="meta"><h3>Direct-Drive PMSG Wind-Turbine Multi-Timescale Modeling &amp; Simulation (in progress)</h3><span class="dates">2026.09 – present</span></div>
      <p class="sub">National Key Laboratory of Renewable Energy Electric Systems, NCEPU — funded undergraduate research project, sole researcher (advised by Dong Zhao, Engineer)</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Hierarchical multi-timescale model of a direct-drive PMSG wind turbine — slow layer (rotor aerodynamics, drivetrain, pitch control; seconds scale), middle layer (DC-link voltage / power / MPPT; hundreds of ms), fast layer (current control, electromagnetic dynamics; ms scale) — for system-level grid-integration simulation on the lab's in-house power-system platform</li>
        <li>Planned sensitivity analysis and singular-perturbation model reduction, with validation against WECC Type 4 and IEC 61400-27-1 (Type 4A/4B) reference models</li>
        <li>Completed: systematic literature review (12 papers on Type 4/4A/4B standards, model-order reduction, LVRT, and primary-frequency-response control) and the overall modeling scheme; ongoing: model derivation, parameter tables, platform implementation, and wind-speed-step / voltage-sag / frequency-disturbance case studies</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="item" id="cfd">
      <div class="meta"><h3>CFD of Cylinder Vibration &amp; Airfoil Dynamic Stall</h3><span class="dates">2026.07 – 2026.08</span></div>
      <p class="sub">Wind Power Research Center, NCEPU — independently completed under doctoral-student supervision</p>
      <p>Five types of two-dimensional cases: cylinder flow and vortex-induced vibration, NACA0012 static aerodynamics and dynamic stall, and S809 dynamic stall. Used <b>ANSYS Fluent</b> as the main solver and ran cylinder flow in <b>OpenFOAM v2512 and v8</b> using Gmsh and ParaView.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Vortex shedding:</b> at Re = 100, captured an alternating vortex street and periodic lift and drag; dimensionless dominant frequencies were approximately <b>0.166 and 0.334</b>, with drag oscillating at about twice the lift frequency.</li>
        <li><b>Cylinder vibration:</b> compared displacement histories and spectra across reduced velocities U* = 7, 8, 9, and 11. Reported transverse amplitudes were approximately 0.42 at U* = 7 and 0.30 at U* = 9; the U* = 11 response decayed over the displayed interval.</li>
        <li><b>Static airfoil loads:</b> with SST k–ω, obtained NACA0012 lift coefficients of approximately <b>1.075 at 10° and 1.469 at 15°</b>; at 20°, lift decreased and force coefficients remained unsteady.</li>
        <li><b>Dynamic stall:</b> compared lift and pitching-moment hysteresis with experimental reference data. NACA0012 (Transition SST) captured the loop shape with deviations near stall and during pitch-down; S809 (GEKO k–ω) followed the pitch-up lift trend but underpredicted lift at intermediate angles during pitch-down.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="project-links"><a class="ref" href="https://github.com/FibreCase/openfoam-cylinder2D" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenFOAM case ↗</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a class="ref" href="/cfd-summary/">Case notes &amp; references</a></p>
      <details class="research-details">
        <summary>View simulation figures and reference context</summary>
        <p class="sub">August 2026 presentation. The figures combine project results with reference curves. These are literature-based simulation cases; experimental data come from published sources.</p>
        <div class="photos two wide">
          <figure class="photo">
            <a class="photo-link" href="/cfd/cylinder-flow.jpg" aria-label="Enlarge: CFD result — flow around a circular cylinder at Re 100, showing the periodic vortex street and lift/drag histories"><img src="/cfd/cylinder-flow.jpg" alt="CFD result — flow around a circular cylinder at Re 100, showing the periodic vortex street and lift/drag histories" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
            <figcaption>Circular cylinder, Re 100 — periodic vortex street; lift/drag histories</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="photo">
            <a class="photo-link" href="/cfd/cylinder-openfoam.jpg" aria-label="Enlarge: CFD result — cylinder flow reproduced in OpenFOAM with the Gmsh / OpenFOAM / ParaView workflow"><img src="/cfd/cylinder-openfoam.jpg" alt="CFD result — cylinder flow reproduced in OpenFOAM with the Gmsh / OpenFOAM / ParaView workflow" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
            <figcaption>Cylinder flow reproduced in OpenFOAM — Gmsh / OpenFOAM / ParaView workflow</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="photo">
            <a class="photo-link" href="/cfd/cylinder-viv.jpg" aria-label="Enlarge: CFD result — vortex-induced vibration of a cylinder: response amplitude across reduced velocities"><img src="/cfd/cylinder-viv.jpg" alt="CFD result — vortex-induced vibration of a cylinder: response amplitude across reduced velocities" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
            <figcaption>Cylinder vibration, Re = 100 — response histories at reduced velocities U* = 7, 8, 9, 11</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="photo">
            <a class="photo-link" href="/cfd/airfoil-naca0012-static.jpg" aria-label="Enlarge: CFD result — NACA0012 static aerodynamics at 10, 15 and 20 degrees with SST k-omega"><img src="/cfd/airfoil-naca0012-static.jpg" alt="CFD result — NACA0012 static aerodynamics at 10, 15 and 20 degrees with SST k-omega" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
            <figcaption>NACA0012 static — lift at 10° / 15° / 20°, SST k-ω</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="photo">
            <a class="photo-link" href="/cfd/airfoil-naca0012-dynamic-stall.jpg" aria-label="Enlarge: CFD result — NACA0012 dynamic stall: lift and pitching-moment hysteresis against experiment"><img src="/cfd/airfoil-naca0012-dynamic-stall.jpg" alt="CFD result — NACA0012 dynamic stall: lift and pitching-moment hysteresis against experiment" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
            <figcaption>NACA0012 dynamic stall — load hysteresis; deviations near stall and during pitch-down</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="photo">
            <a class="photo-link" href="/cfd/airfoil-s809-dynamic-stall.jpg" aria-label="Enlarge: CFD result — S809 dynamic stall: lift curve against experimental reference data"><img src="/cfd/airfoil-s809-dynamic-stall.jpg" alt="CFD result — S809 dynamic stall: lift curve against experimental reference data" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
            <figcaption>S809 dynamic stall — pitch-up trend captured; lift underpredicted during pitch-down</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <p class="reference-note">Reference context: Xintao Li, <cite>Study on the Mechanism of Several Complex Phenomena in Flow-Induced Vibration of Bluff Bodies</cite> (2019), and Jingge Quan, <cite>Study on Aeroelastic Analysis in Separated Flows</cite> (2019), §§3.2.1 and 3.3. The cylinder cases shown here use Re = 100; Li’s §4.3 addresses subcritical Reynolds numbers below approximately 47. Airfoil settings also differ from the source cases.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
